# ADR-013: Oracle AI Decision System

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| ADR | 013 |
| Title | Oracle AI Decision System |
| Status | Accepted |
| Date | 2026-07-27 |
| Decision Makers | R-zension Engineering Team |

---

# Context

Oracle is the intelligence layer of R-zension.

Unlike traditional analytics dashboards that only display numbers, Oracle analyzes platform data to generate insights, recommendations, predictions, and explanations.

The AI system must remain explainable, secure, deterministic where required, and isolated from core business logic.

---

# Decision

Oracle will operate as an independent AI microservice.

The service is responsible for interpreting platform data and generating intelligent recommendations without directly modifying business data.

Oracle is advisory rather than authoritative.

---

# Responsibilities

Oracle is responsible for

- Ranking explanations
- Score explanations
- Performance summaries
- Goal recommendations
- Trend detection
- Predictive analytics
- Insight generation
- AI chat interactions
- Future anomaly detection

Oracle does not

- Modify database records
- Change rankings
- Assign scores
- Authenticate users
- Execute business rules

---

# Architecture

```text
Frontend

↓

Express Backend

↓

Oracle API

↓

LLM Provider

↓

Response

↓

Express

↓

Frontend
```

---

# Communication

Only the Express Backend may communicate with Oracle.

Frontend clients never access Oracle directly.

This centralizes

- Authentication
- Authorization
- Rate limiting
- Logging
- Monitoring

---

# AI Inputs

Oracle may consume

- User profile
- Rankings
- Scores
- Historical activity
- Goals
- Organization settings
- Analytics summaries

Sensitive information should be minimized before transmission.

---

# AI Outputs

Oracle generates

- Explanations
- Recommendations
- Summaries
- Insights
- Predictions

Outputs are informational and must not alter system state automatically.

---

# Prompt Strategy

Prompts should be

- Version controlled
- Reusable
- Modular
- Tested
- Stored outside application logic

Prompt templates should not be hardcoded throughout the codebase.

---

# Explainability

Every recommendation should include sufficient reasoning for users to understand why it was produced.

Oracle should avoid opaque or unsupported conclusions.

---

# Deterministic Operations

Core business logic remains deterministic.

Oracle should never determine

- Official score
- Official rank
- Authorization decisions
- Database updates

These remain the responsibility of backend services.

---

# Failure Handling

If Oracle is unavailable

- Core platform remains operational
- AI features degrade gracefully
- Users receive fallback messaging
- Requests are logged for monitoring

AI failure must not prevent essential platform functionality.

---

# Security

Oracle must

- Receive only necessary data
- Avoid storing sensitive information unnecessarily
- Validate all incoming requests
- Authenticate internal service communication

Prompt injection mitigation should be implemented where applicable.

---

# Performance Goals

| Metric | Target |
|---------|---------|
| AI Request | < 5 seconds |
| Insight Generation | < 3 seconds |
| Service Availability | > 99.5% |

---

# Monitoring

Track

- AI request count
- Token usage
- Latency
- Failure rate
- Provider errors
- Prompt versions
- Cost metrics

---

# Alternatives Considered

## AI Embedded in Backend

Pros

- Fewer services

Cons

- Tight coupling
- Difficult scaling
- Harder maintenance

Decision

Rejected.

---

## Independent AI Service

Pros

- Independent deployment
- Better scalability
- Easier experimentation
- Technology flexibility
- Improved maintainability

Decision

Accepted.

---

# Consequences

Positive

- Loose coupling
- Independent scaling
- Easier provider replacement
- Cleaner architecture
- Better observability

Negative

- Additional infrastructure
- Network latency
- Separate deployment pipeline

---

# Future Evolution

Future enhancements include

- Multiple LLM providers
- Local model support
- Model routing
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)
- Personalized recommendations
- AI memory
- Autonomous analytics agents

---

# Decision Summary

Oracle is implemented as an independent AI microservice responsible for generating explanations, insights, recommendations, and predictions. Business decisions remain under the control of the backend, ensuring transparency, reliability, and maintainability.

